---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ArticleHero from '../../components/ArticleHero.astro';
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Hair Services Guide | Haircuts, Color, Styling & More"
  description="An overview of common hair salon services — haircuts, coloring, styling, treatments, extensions and bridal hair."
  canonicalPath="/hair-services/"
>
  <ArticleHero eyebrow="Hair Services" title="Hair Services" image="/images/gallery/gallery-mens-fade-collage.jpg" imageAlt="Finished fade haircut" />
  <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14">
    <p class="text-xs text-ink/50 mb-2"><a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a> / Hair Services</p>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      A plain-language look at the services you'll commonly find at a salon or salon
      studio, what they involve, and how to decide what's right for you.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      Salon services generally fall into a few broad categories: cutting, coloring,
      styling, treatments, extensions, and occasion-specific services like bridal
      hair. Most people book one service at a time, but many of these naturally
      pair together — a color service is often followed by a cut and blow-dry, for
      instance, and a treatment might be added onto a coloring appointment to
      offset the processing. Each guide below breaks down what the service
      actually involves, what to expect for timing and upkeep, and what's worth
      asking your stylist before you book.
    </p>
    <p class="text-ink/70 mb-8 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      If you're new to a service, start with the guide itself before booking — it
      covers the vocabulary you'll need in a consultation, what a fair timeline
      looks like, and what tends to drive price up or down. That's usually more
      useful than searching photos alone, since a photo shows the result but not
      the process, the maintenance commitment, or what your specific hair type
      might need to do differently to get there.
    </p>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
      <Card title="Haircuts" description="Types of haircuts and how to choose one for your face shape and hair type." href="/hair-services/haircuts/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-mens-fade-collage.jpg" imageAlt="Finished fade haircut" />
      <Card title="Hair Coloring" description="Single-process color, highlights, balayage, ombre and upkeep basics." href="/hair-services/hair-coloring/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-blonde-waves-1.jpg" imageAlt="Blonde balayage color result" />
      <Card title="Hair Styling" description="Blowouts, updos and everyday styling techniques worth knowing." href="/hair-services/hair-styling/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-blonde-waves-2.jpg" imageAlt="Styled hair result" />
      <Card title="Hair Treatments" description="Conditioning, smoothing, and deep-treatment options explained." href="/hair-services/hair-treatments/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-esthetics-room-3.jpg" imageAlt="Private treatment room" />
      <Card title="Hair Extensions" description="Common extension methods, upkeep, and what to ask your stylist." href="/hair-services/hair-extensions/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-private-studio-2.jpg" imageAlt="Private salon studio" />
      <Card title="Bridal Hair" description="Planning timeline and questions for wedding-day hair." href="/hair-services/bridal-hair/" image="/images/gallery/gallery-flowers.jpg" imageAlt="Flowers in a salon setting" />
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-12 mb-3">How to Decide Which Service You Need</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
      If you're not sure where to start, work backward from your goal rather
      than a specific service name. Want a change in shape without changing
      color? That's a cutting question. Want a different overall tone or
      brightness? That's a coloring question, and the specific technique
      (single-process, highlights, balayage) depends on how much contrast and
      maintenance you're comfortable with. Want your hair to feel healthier
      rather than look different? That points toward a treatment rather than a
      cut or color change. Most consultations start with exactly this kind of
      goal-first conversation before narrowing down to a specific service.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Combining Services in One Visit</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Many appointments combine more than one service — a cut with a color, or a
      treatment added onto a chemical service to offset processing. When booking,
      mention every service you're considering upfront rather than adding them
      once you're already in the chair, since your stylist needs to plan the
      full appointment length and product order (color typically happens before
      a cut, for instance) around everything you want done that day.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Booking With Confidence</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Whichever service you're after, walking in with a clear sense of what you
      want — and a realistic idea of timing and cost — tends to produce a
      better result and a smoother appointment than showing up undecided. Use
      these guides, plus our <a href="/tools/salon-cost-calculator/" class="text-rose-600 underline">Salon Cost Calculator</a>,
      to prepare before you book.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Services Evolve Too</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Techniques and product lines change over the years — what's considered a
      standard color technique today may look different from what was popular a
      decade ago. These guides are reviewed periodically to keep terminology
      and recommendations current, so bookmark this hub and check back rather
      than relying on older, unrelated sources for the latest terminology.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">A Note on Pricing Across Services</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      Every guide here touches on pricing to some degree, but none can quote
      exact numbers, since prices vary by professional, region, and current
      demand. Where a guide discusses cost, treat the framing — what drives
      price up or down, what's reasonable to ask about — as more useful than
      any specific dollar figure you might see mentioned elsewhere online.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-3">Start Wherever Makes Sense for You</h2>
    <p class="text-ink/70 leading-relaxed">
      There's no required order to these guides. If you already know which
      service you want, jump straight to that page. If you're still deciding,
      the haircut and hair coloring guides are the two most commonly read
      first, since most other services build on decisions made in one of
      those two categories.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
